    "additionalProperties": false,
    "description": "An append-only CORRECTION of grades already in the log (DATA_MODEL \u00a72.1).\n\nThe ``events`` table is append-only and ``cadus_app`` holds no UPDATE or DELETE on\nit, so a grade recorded in error is not editable. It is superseded instead: this\nevent names the task it corrects and carries the replacement values, and\n:func:`cadus.projector.apply_regrades` folds them onto their targets BEFORE the\nprojector sees the stream. Every derived number \u2014 XP, streak, velocity, the FIRe\nability and memory states \u2014 therefore comes out of the ordinary replay math with\ncorrected inputs. Nothing recomputes a second time and no handler duplicates a rule.\n\nThe correction is written, not derived, and that is the point: the values here are\na dated statement about what the grade should have been, and the original event\nstays in the log beside it. ``reason`` is mandatory so the log says why.\n\n``quality_tier`` / ``xp`` supersede the task's ``lesson_result`` or\n``review_result``; leave both ``None`` to correct attempts only. The result is\nmatched to this task through the attempts that precede it \u2014 see\n:func:`~cadus.projector.apply_regrades` for the matching rule and its limits.",
